# Kotlin: named arguments (Detekt `NamedArguments`)

**`NamedArguments`** (in `config/detekt/detekt.yml`) flags calls with more than **3** unnamed arguments.

## What to do

When a call has several parameters (especially booleans, colours, sizes, or same-typed values), **name them** at the call site — including when the expression already matches the parameter name.

```kotlin
// Prefer
levelBar(
    level = float(Vars.entity(entityId, Vars.KEY_LEVEL)),
    widthDp = widthDp,
    heightDp = C.LEVEL_BAR_HEIGHT_DP,
    fill = color(Vars.tile(tile.id, Vars.KEY_ICON)),
    track = role(Role.TRACK),
    steps = C.LEVEL_STEPS,
) { step -> … }

segmentedLevelBar(
    entityId = entityId,
    levelKey = Vars.KEY_LEVEL,
    widthDp = widthDp,
    heightDp = C.TILE_SEG_BAR_H_DP,
    steps = C.LEVEL_STEPS,
    levelOf = { states -> … },
    fillRole = Role.ACCENT,
    trackRole = Role.TRACK,
) { step -> … }

// Avoid — positional soup past a few args
levelBar(float(…), widthDp, C.LEVEL_BAR_HEIGHT_DP, color(…), role(Role.TRACK), C.LEVEL_STEPS) { … }
```

## Pragmatic limits

- Short calls (≤ 3 args) may stay positional: `gap(C.GAP_10_DP)`, `label(name, Type.BODY, ink)`.
- Trailing lambdas stay trailing; name the parameters *before* the lambda.
- Do not invent names for unused `it` in one-liners.

## After edits

Run `./gradlew :server:detekt` (or the touched module). Prefer fixing call sites you touch.

Existing debt lives in type-specific baselines (`server/detekt-baseline-main.xml`, `…-preview.xml`). Only regenerate after enabling or tightening this rule:

```bash
./gradlew :server:detektBaselineMain :server:detektBaselinePreview
```
